{
	title: './test passes on every run',
	spec: './test is deterministic: run twice on an unchanged tree, it gives the same result. A test that sometimes fails without a bug is deleted, never retried, lengthened or skipped (AGENTS.md). Tests share one bun process, so a test leaves no live state behind: the host fixture (useHost) closes config.ason (config.reset) before deleting its home, or the next config.reset flushes a pending write into a vanished directory and throws.',
	status: 'done',
